045417] [17592186507966 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186507786 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186507966 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186507819 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186507966 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186507858 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186507966 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186507966 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186507966 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186507786 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186507966 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "41b2046a-1076-5804-ad5b-bbdc2b3b7878" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186508047 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186507966 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186508047 #edb/ref 1069 "q-164281" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186508047 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186508047 #edb/ref 1071 "Given the hyperboloid of two sheets $\\frac{{x}^{2}}{3}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{5}-\\frac{(z+1)^{2}}{9}=-1,$ find its $z$-intercepts." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186508047 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "10b62984-455d-5702-af01-c69ee89bcccb" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186508047 #edb/ref 1074 "To find the $z$-intercepts, we plug $x=0$ and $y=0$ into the equation: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{0}^{2}}{3}+\\frac{{0}^{2}}{5}-\\frac{(z+1)^{2}}{9} & =-1 \\\\ -\\frac{(z+1)^{2}}{9} & =-1 \\\\ (z+1)^{2} & =9 \\\\ z+1 & =\\pm 3 \\\\ z & =-1\\pm 3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, we get the solutions $z=-4$ and $z=2.$\n\nTherefore, the intercepts with the $z$-axis are $(0,0,-4)$ and $(0,0,2).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186508091 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186507954 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186508091 #edb/ref 1069 "q-36475" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186508091 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186508091 #edb/ref 1071 "Given the hyperboloid of one sheet  $\\frac{(x-5)^{2}}{9}+\\frac{(y+2)^{2}}{4}-\\frac{(z-3)^{2}}{9}=1$, find its $x$-intercepts." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186508091 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "a868cb2e-b1af-59f1-9123-572788886f02" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186508091 #edb/ref 1074 "To find the $x$-intercepts, we plug $y=0$ and $z=0$ into the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(x-5)^{2}}{9}+\\frac{(0+2)^{2}}{4}-\\frac{(0-3)^{2}}{9} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x-5)^{2}}{9}+1-1 & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x-5)^{2}}{9} & =1 \\\\ (x-5)^{2} & =9 \\\\ x-5 & =\\pm \\sqrt{9} \\\\ x-5 & =\\pm 3 \\\\ x & =5\\pm 3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, we get the solutions $x=2$ and $8.$\n\nTherefore,the intercepts with the $x$-axis are $(2,0,0)$ and $(8,0,0).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
